# 113. CORE SYNCHRONIZATION RULES

```text
RULE 01
All rewards must pass through Reward Processor.

RULE 02
Reward calculation must not be duplicated
by Inventory or Currency systems.

RULE 03
Currency belongs to Currency Account.

RULE 04
Gem belongs to Currency Account.

RULE 05
Recruit Ticket belongs to Ticket Account
or Currency Account according to configuration.

RULE 06
Resources belong to Resource Account or Inventory
according to item configuration.

RULE 07
Items belong to Inventory.

RULE 08
Quest Progress belongs to Quest System.

RULE 09
Dungeon Progress belongs to Dungeon System.

RULE 10
Recruitment Cost belongs to Recruitment Processor.

RULE 11
Recruitment Result belongs to Recruitment Processor.

RULE 12
RNG Result belongs to RNG System.

RULE 13
Game State stores synchronized final state.

RULE 14
Database stores persistent state.

RULE 15
Every reward transaction requires a unique ID.

RULE 16
Every reward source requires a source ID.

RULE 17
Every recruitment request requires a unique ID.

RULE 18
Every transaction must support rollback.

RULE 19
Duplicate reward distribution is forbidden.

RULE 20
Partial reward commit is forbidden for atomic transactions.

RULE 21
Recruitment cannot proceed if Gem or Ticket is insufficient.

RULE 22
Insufficient resource errors must not deduct any resource.

RULE 23
Insufficient resource errors must not execute RNG.

RULE 24
Concurrent Recruitment requests must use resource locking.

RULE 25
Currency balance must be read from the authoritative account.
```

